A filter ADR-0017 specified, four docstrings described as live, and nothing ever
called. Added 2026-05-14 with ZERO production callers; its only reachability was
five unit tests, which is precisely what held it at 100% coverage and kept it
invisible. The contract it was written for was implemented by a DIFFERENT
function — _lookup_named_entry filtering with io_boundary._module_matches — and
the two drifted: the live one was bidirectional SUBSTRING containment until
WI-zazul and ungated resolved first-party edges entirely until WI-damir.

HARVESTED BEFORE DELETING. The dead function was MORE CORRECT on one point: it
exempted both `external` and `<external>` from module filtering, per ADR-0017
§3a, while the live path tested only the bare spelling. So an `<external>` hint
fell into the module-FILTER branch and was compared as though it were a real
module name — matching nothing and SUPPRESSING the finding, the opposite of the
ADR's "degrade to short-name matching, because rejecting outright would suppress
legitimate findings". Both spellings now live in one
_UNRESOLVED_MODULE_PLACEHOLDERS frozenset, which is what stops the pair drifting
apart again.

MEASURED: zero cohort change (272 flows / 13 non-realizable, 0 added, 0 removed
across the same 9 repos). The instrument check asserts the exemption is ACTIVE
before measuring, so this is a real null and not a stale read — `<external>`
occurs in that corpus as flow SEED symbols rather than as callee module hints
reaching the matcher. Practical impact on real corpora is UNMEASURED, NOT ZERO.
This PR rests on ADR conformance, a unit test, and deleting a filter that never
ran — not on a measured improvement.

FOUR DOCSTRINGS DESCRIBED A MECHANISM THAT DOES NOT RUN, including
taint_refine.py's MODULE docstring, whose stated reason for that pass existing
was "the rewritten dst then participates in _sink_module_compatible directly".
The pass has a real effect, through a different consumer with different
semantics, so anyone reading it to learn what module strings must look like
reasoned about the wrong predicate. L50 at the largest scale it has appeared:
not a comment justifying a boundary, but a module's stated purpose.

ADR-0017 AMENDED IN PLACE at three sites (docs/adr/README.md: ADRs are edited in
place, git history is the record): §3a names the real filter and carries a dated
correction; the per-language section no longer attributes the work to the dead
function; and §"Production deployments" no longer claims hypergumbo's own
self-audit runs "sink-module-compatibility filtering", which was false.

The real ADR-0037 debt is now filed rather than implied (WI-lonad): both
invalidation markers say "implementing fixes will re-key sink matching and
refinement on dst_ref", and dst_ref appears 14 times in ir.py and ZERO times in
taint.py.

